          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: обследовать",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "обследовать (obslédovat) — \"to examine (medically)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Врач внимательно обследовал пациента. Vrach vnimátelno obslédoval patsiyénta. The doctor examined the patient carefully."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective and perfective (one form for both). Present обследую."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "обследовать (obslédovat) is built on об- and следовать 'to follow', from след 'track, trail' (EtymDB lists all three without a source)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
